{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":76100,"duration_api_ms":75412,"num_turns":3,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ad6f9d9b-8a56-452b-b7c5-5664c01597a3","total_cost_usd":0.34623080000000006,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24101,"cache_read_input_tokens":78147,"output_tokens":1518,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24101,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":1518,"cacheReadInputTokens":78147,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24101,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.22767475,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":75,"outputTokens":3653,"cacheReadInputTokens":269098,"cacheCreationInputTokens":58645,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11855605000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments make factual claims that are contradicted by the current codebase. Denitrification is fully implemented: nitrogen_cycle.rs includes a complete denitrification phase (lines 508-579) with Monod kinetics for NO3/DOC, suboxic pore volume dependence, and alkalinity production; process.rs defines all denitrification parameters with defaults; default.toml includes corresponding values; budget.rs tracks cumulative_n2_export_mg_n; biology.rs has denitrifier_activity_index; and denitrification.rs contains 12 comprehensive tests. The planner positions correctly identify these facts.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-325f0882","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment claims step_nitrogen_cycle only runs feed leaching, mineralization, and nitrification, and that nitrate is never reduced to N2. This is factually wrong. nitrogen_cycle.rs lines 508-579 implement a complete denitrification phase: it computes suboxic_pore_volume_l from substrate geometry, applies Monod factors for NO3 (k_no3) and DOC (k_doc), scales by denitrifier_activity_index from biology.rs, removes nitrate, tracks N2 export via cumulative_n2_export_mg_n, and returns alkalinity via DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N. The substrate.rs file does expose suboxic-zone geometry (SubstrateZone::Suboxic, suboxic_pore_volume_cm3(), suboxic_depth_cm()) and the denitrifier state lives in biology.rs, not substrate.rs. The amendment's core factual claims do not match the code."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-a56c3028","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment claims denitrification parameters and defaults are missing from process.rs and default.toml. This is incorrect. process.rs defines denitrification_vmax_mg_n_per_l_per_hour, denitrification_k_no3_mg_n_per_l, denitrification_k_doc_mg_c_per_l, denitrification_pore_water_mixing_factor, and denitrification_activity_maturation_days (lines 142-175), each with a corresponding default function (lines 490-516). default.toml also contains all five denitrification defaults (lines 90-98) with documented stoichiometry. The amendment describes a state of the code that does not exist."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-4cbac42a","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment claims N2 export accounting is not wired and denitrification would be treated as an unexplained nitrogen leak. This is wrong. The implementation tracks denitrification exports explicitly through cumulative_n2_export_mg_n, which is included in the nitrogen budget components array in budget.rs (line 345), ensuring the nitrogen conservation check accounts for gas-phase export. Additionally, a dedicated test file crates/tank_core/tests/denitrification.rs exists with 12 tests covering NO3 removal, N2 export tracking, alkalinity production, Monod kinetics, suboxic volume scaling, activity maturation, and budget balance. The claim that test coverage only covers nitrification/alkalinity is false."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"49a5b687-068b-4ab6-8e99-ae0bd5bca878"}
